WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.010
Communication and documentation run through the entire incident response lifecycle.

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:08.702
They are how teams keep technical work, business decisions, and accountability aligned.

00:00:08.702 --> 00:00:13.003
Useful records include timelines, evidence references, affected assets, owners, decisions made,

00:00:13.003 --> 00:00:16.131
approvals, actions taken, open questions, and known assumptions.

00:00:16.131 --> 00:00:18.086
Different audiences need different detail.

00:00:18.086 --> 00:00:20.823
Analysts may need log references and hypotheses.

00:00:20.823 --> 00:00:23.950
Executives may need impact, risk, and next decisions.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.860
Legal and privacy teams may need data categories, notification considerations,

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.033
and preservation status.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:32.161
System owners need practical recovery and validation steps.

00:00:32.161 --> 00:00:34.507
Good communication is clear about uncertainty.

00:00:34.507 --> 00:00:37.635
It should not overstate what the team knows,

00:00:37.635 --> 00:00:40.372
and it should not hide material risk.

00:00:40.372 --> 00:00:43.891
Lessons learned are the bridge from response to improvement.

00:00:43.891 --> 00:00:48.583
A post-incident review should identify what worked, what slowed the team down,

00:00:48.583 --> 00:00:53.666
which detections or logs were missing, whether access or backups behaved as expected,

00:00:53.666 --> 00:00:55.621
and what playbooks need updates.

00:00:55.621 --> 00:00:57.576
The goal is not blame.

00:00:57.576 --> 00:01:01.486
The goal is a concrete improvement plan with owners, deadlines,

00:01:01.486 --> 00:01:05.786
and evidence that the organization will be better prepared next time.

00:01:05.786 --> 00:01:10.478
Documentation should be written as the response unfolds, not reconstructed entirely afterward.

00:01:10.478 --> 00:01:12.824
Time stamps, decision owners, evidence locations,

00:01:12.824 --> 00:01:17.125
and open questions are much easier to capture in the moment.

00:01:17.125 --> 00:01:21.426
Clear notes also protect the team from confusion when shifts change,

00:01:21.426 --> 00:01:26.900
leaders ask for updates, or a later review examines why a decision was made.
